---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const domainColor = '#ec4899'; // Pink for Aggregate Reporting
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Aggregate Reporting Agent — Medivora"
  description="Architecture and capabilities of the Medivora Aggregate Reporting Agent for automating PSUR, DSUR, and PBRER drafting."
>
  <article class="agent-detail-page">
    
    <!-- ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <header class="agent-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/agents">← Back to Agents</a>
        </div>
        
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span class="domain-tag" style={`--dc: ${domainColor}`}>Pharmacovigilance</span>
          <span class="phase-tag">Phase 4 · Reporting</span>
          <span class="date-tag">Last reviewed: Jun 2025</span>
        </div>
        
        <h1 class="agent-title">Aggregate Reporting Agent</h1>
        <p class="agent-tagline">Automated synthesis of line listings for PSURs, DSURs, and PBRERs.</p>

        <div class="agent-hero-pattern" style="--agent-accent: rgba(139,92,246,0.12)"></div>
        
        <div class="reading-meta">
          <span class="reading-meta-item">📖 11 min read</span>
          <span class="reading-meta-item">📅 Updated 2025-06-02</span>
          <button class="btn-print" onclick="window.print()">🖨 Save as PDF</button>
        </div>

        <nav class="pipeline-indicator" aria-label="ICSR Pipeline Position">
          <a href="/agents/intake-triage" class="pipeline-step">Intake</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/meddra-coding" class="pipeline-step">Coding</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/medical-review" class="pipeline-step">Review</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/aggregate-reporting" class="pipeline-step active">Reporting</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/literature-monitoring" class="pipeline-step">Literature</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/regulatory-intelligence" class="pipeline-step">RegIntel</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="agent-metrics">
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">40<sup>[1]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">Hours saved per PSUR generation</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">95%<sup>[2]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">First-draft acceptance rate</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">100%<sup>[3]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">ICH E2C(R2) format compliance</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:1.5rem; padding-top:1rem; border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);">
          <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.62rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.4); margin-bottom:0.6rem;">References & Sources</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[1] McKinsey & Company, 'GenAI in Pharma Operations', 2024 <span class="risk-med" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Projected)</span></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[2] Deloitte, 'Automating Aggregate Reporting', 2024 <span class="risk-med" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Projected)</span></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[3] ICH E2C(R2) Guideline, Step 4 Version <span class="" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Design Principle)</span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="reviewed-by-band">
          <div class="rb-icon">✓</div>
          <div class="rb-text">
            Content reviewed by <strong>Kritnandan</strong>, B.Tech BSBE (IIT Kanpur) | Last review: Jun 2025 | Review cadence: Quarterly
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ── THE PROBLEM ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-light problem-section">
      <div class="wrap content-grid">
        <div class="cg-main">
          <h2>The Copy-Paste Dilemma</h2>
          <p class="lead-text">
            Writing a Periodic Safety Update Report (PSUR) or a Development Safety Update Report (DSUR) is a grueling exercise in copy-pasting. Medical writers spend weeks pulling line listings from the safety database, formatting tables, and manually summarizing thousands of adverse events into cohesive narratives.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Medivora Aggregate Reporting Agent automates the heavy lifting. It interfaces directly with the safety database, executes complex queries to generate summary tabulations, and uses an LLM to draft the narrative sections, allowing medical writers to act as high-level editors rather than data gatherers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="cg-side info-panel">
          <h4>Agent Profile</h4>
          <dl class="agent-specs">
            <dt>Data Inputs</dt>
            <dd>Safety database line listings, previous PSURs, risk management plans (RMP).</dd>
            <dt>Core AI Models</dt>
            <dd>Long-context LLMs for document generation, strict Data Analysts for table generation.</dd>
            <dt>Key Outputs</dt>
            <dd>Pre-drafted Word/PDF PSUR, PBRER, and DSUR documents.</dd>
            <dt>Standards</dt>
            <dd>ICH E2C (R2), EMA GVP Module VII.</dd>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── ARCHITECTURE ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark arch-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Agent Architecture &amp; Workflow</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Because aggregate reports require absolute data fidelity, the agent separates the table generation (handled by deterministic SQL scripts) from the narrative generation (handled by the LLM), fusing them together at the final step.
        </p>
        
        <div class="diagram-container">
          <pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    classDef external fill:#1a1a1a,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px,color:#888
    classDef input fill:#112a22,stroke:#ec4899,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef agent fill:#0a192f,stroke:#64ffda,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef db fill:#2d1b2e,stroke:#e05c8a,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef hitl fill:#3a2a00,stroke:#e8a838,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef output fill:#112a22,stroke:#ec4899,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff

    subgraph "Data Sources"
        direction TB
        SafetyDB[("Argus/Vault<br>Safety Database")]:::external
        PrevDoc["Previous PSUR<br>(For context)"]:::external
    end

    subgraph "Generation Layer"
        direction TB
        TableAgent["Data & Table Agent<br>(SQL / Deterministic)"]:::input
        NarrativeAgent(["Narrative Drafting Agent<br>(LLM)"]):::agent
        Compiler["Document Compiler<br>(Word / PDF)"]:::agent
    end

    subgraph "Review Layer"
        direction TB
        Writer["Medical Writer<br>(Editor)"]:::hitl
        FinalDoc["Submission-Ready<br>Aggregate Report"]:::output
    end

    SafetyDB --> TableAgent
    SafetyDB --> NarrativeAgent
    PrevDoc --> NarrativeAgent

    TableAgent -- "Summary Tabulations" --> Compiler
    NarrativeAgent -- "Draft Text Sections" --> Compiler

    Compiler --> Writer
    Writer -- "Final Edits" --> FinalDoc

    linkStyle default stroke:#444,stroke-width:2px;
          </pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CORE CAPABILITIES ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-light caps-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-title-dark">Core Capabilities</h2>
        <div class="caps-grid">
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">1</div>
            <h3>Automated Summary Tabulations</h3>
            <p>Generates complex, multi-layered tables required by ICH E2C (R2), pulling directly from the safety database to eliminate transcription and mathematical errors.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">2</div>
            <h3>Interval vs. Cumulative Analysis</h3>
            <p>Automatically calculates the differences between the current reporting interval and the cumulative data, highlighting new trends or unexpected shifts in reporting frequencies.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">3</div>
            <h3>Section-by-Section Drafting</h3>
            <p>Drafts narrative text for sections like 'Patient Exposure', 'Presentation of Safety Data', and 'Benefit-Risk Analysis', mimicking the company's approved medical writing style.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">4</div>
            <h3>Traceability Links</h3>
            <p>Every claim made in the generated text (e.g., "There were 14 cases of anaphylaxis") contains a hyperlink back to the source line-listing query, making QC/QA review incredibly fast.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
    <!-- ── UNDER THE HOOD ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark under-hood-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Under the Hood</span>
        <h2>Architectural Deep Dive</h2>
        
        <div class="uh-grid">
          <div class="uh-col">
            <h3>Massive Context Window Orchestration</h3>
            <p>Drafting a PSUR requires synthesizing thousands of individual cases. The agent utilizes Map-Reduce architectures and Long-Context LLMs (e.g., Claude 3.5 Sonnet or Gemini 1.5 Pro) to summarize cases by System Organ Class (SOC) before drafting the final narrative.</p>
            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
              <div class="code-header"><span class="code-dot r"></span><span class="code-dot y"></span><span class="code-dot g"></span><span class="code-title">map_reduce_flow.py</span></div>
              <pre is:raw><code># 1. Map Phase: Summarize cases per SOC
soc_summaries = []
for soc, cases in grouped_cases.items():
    prompt = f"Summarize the safety profile for SOC {soc}. Cases: {cases}"
    summary = llm.generate(prompt)
    soc_summaries.append(summary)

# 2. Reduce Phase: Draft final section
final_prompt = f"""
Draft Section 16.1 (Summary of Safety Concerns) 
using the following SOC summaries: {soc_summaries}
"""
final_draft = llm.generate(final_prompt)</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="uh-col">
            <h3>Medical Writing Style Prompts</h3>
            <p>The agent is heavily prompted to adopt the specific tone and structural constraints required by ICH E2C (R2) guidelines for Periodic Benefit-Risk Evaluation Reports.</p>
            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
              <div class="code-header"><span class="code-dot r"></span><span class="code-dot y"></span><span class="code-dot g"></span><span class="code-title">system_prompt.txt</span></div>
              <pre is:raw><code>You are an expert Medical Writer drafting a PSUR/PBRER.

WRITING CONSTRAINTS:
1. Tone: Formal, objective, data-driven.
2. Structure: Follow ICH E2C (R2) format exactly.
3. Denominators: Always state the number of cases vs. the estimated patient exposure.
4. Cumulative Data: Clearly distinguish between the current reporting interval and cumulative data.
5. Actionability: Highlight if a new safety signal was identified during the interval.

Do not use colloquialisms. Avoid redundant phrasing.</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guardrails-box">
          <h3>Guardrails & Failure Modes</h3>
          <ul class="guardrail-list">
            <li><strong>Data/Narrative Mismatch:</strong> The LLM's generated narrative might state "There were 15 cases of rash" while the appended statistical table shows 16. A separate "Validation Agent" strictly compares the drafted text against the source JSON tables to catch mismatches.</li>
            <li><strong>Loss in the Middle:</strong> When fed thousands of pages of line listings, some LLMs suffer from "lost in the middle" syndrome, ignoring cases in the center of the prompt. Map-reduce chunking is required to prevent this.</li>
            <li><strong>Benefit-Risk Assessment:</strong> The final determination of the Benefit-Risk profile is a complex, highly nuanced medical decision. The agent can draft the summary of evidence, but the final conclusion remains strictly human.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  
    <!-- ── SAMPLE DEMO ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
